%% Architecture sequence: real index-time and query-time ownership plus the release boundary.
%% Sources: EV-T4-001..EV-T4-012 (pinned SHAs llama_index@d8021225, haystack@c7cb46c0);
%% release boundary per src/rag_compare/release.py and failure injection (artifacts/results/failure-injection.json).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Corpus (v1/v2 .md)
    participant R as Release layer (framework-independent)
    participant SHARED as Shared layer (parse/split/identity)
    participant LI as LlamaIndex adapter
    participant HI as Haystack adapter
    participant OL as Ollama (nomic-embed-text / qwen3:4b-instruct)
    participant Q as Query caller

    rect rgb(235, 245, 255)
    Note over C,R: Index-time — staging namespace created, index built, THEN validated at promotion
    C->>R: corpus files + manifest.json (source_id, hashes)
    R->>R: stage_release: copy corpus into immutable staging namespace; write chunk inventory + release manifest
    SHARED->>SHARED: parse + real cl100k_base token-window split (200/40) + identity contract (src/rag_compare/adapters/base.py, tests/test_chunking.py)

    alt LlamaIndex index path
        R->>LI: build_release(corpus_path, manifest, trace)
        LI->>LI: index shared chunks as TextNodes with pre-computed embeddings; node ids = contract chunk ids (EV-T4-001)
        LI->>OL: embeddings already attached (no Settings fallback, no re-embed) (EV-T4-002/004/005)
    else Haystack index path
        R->>HI: build_release(corpus_path, manifest, trace)
        HI->>HI: chunks indexed verbatim as Documents (id/text/embedding/meta from contract); no framework-native splitting (HS-1/HS-2 DuplicatePolicy.FAIL)
    end

    R->>R: validate_release: file set, SHA-256 hashes, counts, schema, embedding identity, QUERY CONTRACT (retriever/rerank/packing/generator/prompt/options) + stored chunk inventory recomputed from corpus bytes (release.py)
    R->>R: promote_release: validate staging == manifest, then ONE atomic os.replace of active pointer
    R-->>R: failed validation never touches active.json (Task 7 rev: partial v2 rejected on BOTH adapters, pointer stayed {"release_id": "v1"})
    end

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
    Note over Q,OL: Query-time — release captured ONCE at query start
    Q->>R: capture_active_release() -> release_id pinned for this query
    Q->>LI: query(text, retriever_kind, active_release, trace)
    Q->>HI: query(text, retriever_kind, active_release, trace)

    par LlamaIndex retrieve (EV-T4-008/LI-8)
        LI->>OL: embed query (explicit model) or BM25 via store
        OL-->>LI: query vector
        LI->>LI: VectorStoreRetriever._retrieve top_k=5, ordered by store score
    and Haystack retrieve (HS-6..HS-10)
        HI->>HI: Pipeline.run explicit graph; BM25 in store (scale_score=False) or dense w/ filters
        HI->>OL: embed query for ollama_dense branch
        OL-->>HI: query vector
    end

    LI->>LI: filter_chunks_for_release(release_id) - raises MixedReleaseError on foreign chunk
    HI->>HI: filter_chunks_for_release(release_id) - same shared control
    LI->>OL: generate (temperature 0, prompt sha e029718b…)
    HI->>OL: generate (same prompt, same budget 1200 tokens)
    LI->>LI: citation stage: resolve answer [n] markers to contract chunk ids
    HI->>HI: same citation stage (separately traced after generate)
    OL-->>Q: answer + citations (source_id_and_chunk_id mode); every chunk carries provenance + release_id
    end
